Feature: Compositing Preview — Asset Superimposed on Video Scene
  As an editor reviewing placements
  I want to preview how a brand asset looks composited onto a detected surface in the video
  So that I can verify the placement looks realistic before approving it for rendering

  Background:
    Given the BIT platform has detected surfaces in video content
    And brand assets have been placed on surfaces
    And the compositing engine is configured via Platform Settings

  Scenario: Preview places asset at the correct surface location
    Given a surface with valid boundary coordinates has a placed asset
    When I click "🎬 Composite Preview"
    Then the asset image is superimposed onto the video frame at the surface location
    And the resulting image shows the video scene with the asset overlaid
    And the asset fills the surface bounding box

  Scenario: Preview works with any image asset format
    Given a surface has a placed asset of type PNG, JPG, or GIF
    When I request a composite preview
    Then the asset is correctly overlaid on the video frame
    And the result is returned as a base64-encoded PNG image

  Scenario: Preview fails gracefully when asset file is missing
    Given a surface has a placed asset whose file does not exist on disk
    When I request a composite preview
    Then an error is returned with a clear message
    And the error does not crash the API

  Scenario: Preview fails gracefully when video file is missing
    Given a content item whose video file does not exist on disk
    When I request a composite preview for a surface on that content
    Then an error is returned indicating the video file is missing

  Scenario: Preview uses the configured compositing engine
    Given the platform setting "engine_compositing" is set to "opencv"
    When a composite preview is requested
    Then FFmpeg is used to extract the video frame and overlay the asset
    And the result engine reports "OpenCvCompositor"

  Scenario: Basic engine falls back to raw asset only
    Given the platform setting "engine_compositing" is set to "basic"
    When a composite preview is requested
    Then the raw asset image is returned without scene compositing
    And the result engine reports "BasicCompositor"
